{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"747287820221284362","content":"Just so you all know, and would likely take a convo with radar to make sure it would be appropriate, but DDB just added the ability to grant spells to your spell list (like the rav ones) via homebrew backgrounds.  So for instance, if you wanted something like \"Disciple of Sandigil\" (not saying this is a background, just what came to my head as an example of a background that might have inherent ties to a spell), you could just grant access to goodberry, and thus a wizard could have goodberry on their spell list.  They would still have to add it to their book and mem it, its not free, but possible.","created_at":"2020-08-24T20:38:07.702000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747555364072849441","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
